Mode meanings
ADC
Copies normalized VAL into OUT, in both integer and floating-point matrices. code_menu.cpp (lines 258-262)

Trigger
Uses high and low thresholds as hysteresis:

VAL >= high threshold and trigger not latched
    -> emit current random value
    -> record external-clock time
    -> latch trigger

VAL <= low threshold
    -> clear latch
This creates a sample-and-hold–like random event source driven by an analog threshold crossing. code_menu.cpp (lines 264-279)

LFO modes
Route the globally calculated LFO 1 or LFO 2 value into the selected channel’s output. code_menu.cpp (lines 281-291)

Audio modes
Route one of four derived audio-band values into the selected channel’s output. code_menu.cpp (lines 293-315)

