The eight processed channels do not only become arbitrary shader parameters. Selected channels also control higher-level rendering targets.

applyTargetModes() handles:

shader program selection;
texture selection;
video selection;
frame selection;
shader-time selection. code_menu.cpp (lines 317-368)
Program selection
In performance layer 0, analog channel 7 is mapped across the number of valid fragment shaders. The SEL_PRG state functions as pickup/permission behavior before the current OpenGL program follows the physical selector. code_menu.cpp (lines 319-334)

Texture selection
SEL_TEX identifies a channel used to determine m_activeTex, scaled over the number of valid textures. code_menu.cpp (lines 336-342)

Video and frame selection
