The four LEDs correspond naturally to each four-setting menu block.

The LED update code maps menu layers to blocks, obtains either output values or the four settings in the selected block, and uses the color table to display state. The layer-to-block relationship begins in updateLED(). code_menu.cpp (lines 370-407)

This makes the LED strip a compact hardware UI:

LED A <-> first item/knob in selected layer
LED B <-> second item/knob
LED C <-> third item/knob
LED D <-> fourth item/knob
In performance mode the LEDs can visualize channel output levels. In menu mode they can represent the values/modes of the selected four-item block.

That aligns the entire interface around groups of four:

4 menu controls
4 LEDs
4-value mode blocks
4-value GLSL vectors
