20. Final evaluation
The first implementation
The original build was successful in the most important experimental sense:

It proved that a Circle bare-metal Raspberry Pi application could import shared buffers into VCSM, configure the VideoCore MMAL H.264 decoder, submit encoded data, receive a decoded frame as a GPU-accessible texture, and display it through the application’s shader renderer.

That is a genuine result.

Its weakness was not failure to decode. Its weakness was that the critical mechanism lived behind experimental addon classes and remained difficult to reason about when the system developed a delayed runtime failure.

The current implementation
The current build is a deeper technical accomplishment:

It converts the working experiment into an explicit model of the underlying firmware protocols, memory domains, media framing, buffer lifecycle, and application state.

It has not yet regained all of the first build’s runtime connectivity, but it has gained something more strategically valuable: the code now owns the knowledge needed to diagnose and control the entire path.

